ssuecomment-3835803083","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115696","id":3835803083,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kobXL","user":{"login":"brendevr","id":178747313,"node_id":"U_kgDOCqd3sQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/178747313?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brendevr","html_url":"https://github.com/brendevr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brendevr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brendevr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brendevr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brendevr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brendevr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brendevr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brendevr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brendevr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brendevr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-02T15:20:03Z","updated_at":"2026-02-02T15:20:03Z","body":"From a high level view, I was trying to think of the “best” solution. My issue with the Polygon2D dock (and this may be subjective, but worthy of discussion) is that it is redundant, you can configure everything you want about points in the Editor View, the Polygon2D dock offers the exact same behavior but in a dock at the bottom. Compare this with the TileMap dock, it offers behavior and functions not available anywhere else, thus the dock should open.\r\nHowever, I have realized in writing this that it would make more sense for all of these node-specific docks to respect pin state, so I will work on generalizing it.\r\nAlso, code-wise, I will check out those things you pointed out and implement them.\r\nThanks.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/383